From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Pfeiffer <cpfeiffer@rev-crew.info>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:43:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Fix SDK Hooks growing the game's entity listeners with
 the wrong heap

SDK Hooks adds itself to the game's entity listeners,
CGlobalEntityList's CUtlVector<IEntityListener *>, with AddToTail.
CUtlMemory grows with plain malloc and realloc. The game's libraries
route those to tier0 (memoverride.cpp), but SourceMod's extensions
don't link it, so a growth in the extension comes from the C runtime's
heap. If that happens, the vector's block is the C runtime's, and the
game hands it to tier0 the next time it grows the vector.

When SDK Hooks loads at the server's start, i.e. a plugin loaded then
uses it, the vector is still empty, and SDK Hooks makes its first
allocation. CUtlMemory's first allocation is 32 bytes, whatever the
size of the elements: 8 pointers on x86, 4 on x86_64. Whether the game
then grows the vector depends on how many listeners it adds. Day of
Infamy adds 5 more until its first map has started:
- On x86, 6 listeners fit into the 8 slots, the game never grows the
  vector, and the C runtime's block goes unnoticed.
- On x86_64, the fifth listener doesn't fit into 4 slots: the game grows
  the vector at the map start, tier0's realloc gets the C runtime's
  block, which it takes for one of its own, and the server crashes.

So the crash on x86_64 Windows comes from the vector's size alone; a
game that adds more listeners would hand the C runtime's block to
tier0 on x86 as well. Loaded later, the vector already holds the game's
listeners in tier0's block, with room for SDK Hooks'.

Grow the vector with g_pMemAlloc->Realloc before adding the listener,
so its block is always tier0's.

To reproduce, on Day of Infamy's 64-bit Windows server (srcds_x64),
load a plugin at startup that only includes <sdkhooks> and does
nothing: the server crashes at the map start. With full page heap
(gflags /p /enable srcds_x64.exe /full) the crash points at the block's
allocation in SDKHooks::SDK_OnLoad. Under a debugger, with write
breakpoints on the vector's fields, stock SourceMod shows on both
servers: an empty vector when SDK_OnLoad runs; SDK Hooks' allocation of
8 slots (x86) or 4 (x86_64); the game's 5 listeners after it; on x86_64
the access violation in tier0 as the fifth is added, on x86 no
reallocation at all.

Tested on Windows 11 with SourceMod built with MSVC 14.52 (Visual
Studio 2026): the reproducer crashes with master at the map start,
leaving a crash dump, and runs with this patch alone. With the whole
series, the server runs with all of SourceMod's extensions and 25
plugins loaded, on 64-bit (also under full page heap) and on 32-bit.
---
 extensions/sdkhooks/extension.cpp | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/extensions/sdkhooks/extension.cpp b/extensions/sdkhooks/extension.cpp
index be521479..527130d6 100644
--- a/extensions/sdkhooks/extension.cpp
+++ b/extensions/sdkhooks/extension.cpp
@@ -126,6 +126,31 @@ IForward *g_pOnLevelInit = NULL;
 
 IGameConfig *g_pGameConf = NULL;
 
+// Adds a listener to the game's entity listeners, growing their vector with the game's allocator,
+// tier0's: CUtlVector grows with malloc and realloc, which the game's libraries route to tier0
+// (memoverride.cpp) but SourceMod's extensions don't. While the vector is empty or full, e.g. when the
+// extension loads at the server's start, the C runtime's block would be the vector's, which the game's
+// next growth hands to tier0's realloc: a block that allocator never made.
+void AddGameEntityListener(CUtlVector<IEntityListener *> *listeners, IEntityListener *listener)
+{
+	struct Access : CUtlVector<IEntityListener *>
+	{
+		static CUtlMemory<IEntityListener *> &Memory(CUtlVector<IEntityListener *> *vector)
+		{
+			return static_cast<Access *>(vector)->m_Memory;
+		}
+	};
+	CUtlMemory<IEntityListener *> &memory = Access::Memory(listeners);
+	if (listeners->Count() >= memory.NumAllocated())
+	{
+		int count = memory.NumAllocated() > 0 ? memory.NumAllocated() * 2 : 4;
+		IEntityListener **elements = memory.Detach();
+		elements = (IEntityListener **)g_pMemAlloc->Realloc(elements, count * sizeof(IEntityListener *));
+		memory.AssumeMemory(elements, count);
+	}
+	listeners->AddToTail(listener);
+}
+
 CUtlVector<IEntityListener *> *EntListeners()
 {
 	void *gEntList = gamehelpers->GetGlobalEntityList();
@@ -241,7 +266,7 @@ bool SDKHooks::SDK_OnLoad(char *error, size_t maxlength, bool late)
 	}
 	else
 	{
-		entListeners->AddToTail(this);
+		AddGameEntityListener(entListeners, this);
 	}
 
 
